  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5054",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a potential modulator of BE-13 through a shared pathway involving palmarumycin CP18. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N directly targets A704, which is a target of palmarumycin CP18, and that palmarumycin CP18, in turn, targets BE-13. This indicates a potential mechanism where Mollicellin N may influence the activity of palmarumycin CP18, which then affects BE-13. The scores from the three paths suggest a consistent level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction between Mollicellin N and palmarumycin CP18 remains unclear. The presence of multiple overlapping targets (A704, Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, and P2X purinoceptor 1) further supports the idea that Mollicellin N may act through a broader biological network, potentially influencing multiple pathways that ultimately lead to the modulation of BE-13. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of understanding the molecular interactions between these compounds to elucidate their potential therapeutic applications.",
